<% content_for :title, "Privacy Policy: Pangu Terminal" %>
<% content_for :description, "What Pangu Terminal stores, which services process it, and how to delete your account." %>
<%= main_content_frame do %>
  <article class="legal-page">
    <h1 class="legal-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="legal-meta">Last updated 2026-10-24</p>

    <p>Pangu Terminal is a free, fan-made planning tool for Wuthering Waves, run by one person. It is not affiliated with Kuro Games. This page says what the app stores and why. We do not sell data, show ads or track you across other sites.</p>

    <h2>Signing in</h2>
    <p>You can sign in with Google or Discord. We ask each provider only for your basic profile and use just the provider account ID. We do not request your email address, and we do not store your provider name or profile picture. You get a random username, such as <code>rover-4821</code>, which is shown in the navigation bar and which you can change in Account Settings. Older accounts created with an email address and password keep that email and a hashed password; the email is used only to sign in and to send a password reset.</p>

    <h2>What we store</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Your account: username, provider and provider account ID, and your SOL3 phase setting.</li>
      <li>Your plans, inventory quantities and API keys (API keys are stored only as hashes).</li>
      <li>If you use the planner without an account: your plans, tied to a random token in a cookie in your browser.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Sharing a plan</h2>
    <p>If you choose to share a plan, the app creates a random link. Anyone who has the link can see that one plan and its material totals. The page shows no name, email, username or inventory, and search engines are asked not to list it. You can stop sharing at any time, which turns the link off, and deleting the plan does the same.</p>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>The app sets a session cookie to keep you signed in, an optional "remember me" cookie for older email accounts, and a guest cookie for guest plans. We do not use advertising or analytics cookies.</p>

    <h2>Services that process data</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Google and Discord authenticate you when you choose to sign in with them.</li>
      <li>Render hosts the app and Neon hosts the database. Like most hosts, they keep standard request logs, which include IP addresses.</li>
      <li>Postmark delivers password-reset emails to older email accounts.</li>
      <li>The Farming Advisor sends Google's Gemini model a list of materials, quantities and farming estimates. It does not send your name, account ID or email.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
    <p>Open Account Settings and choose Delete Account. This permanently removes your account, linked sign-in methods, plans, inventory and API keys. Guest plans can be removed by clearing your cookies, and unclaimed guest plans are pruned after a period of inactivity.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions or deletion requests: <a href="mailto:pangu-terminal-support@googlegroups.com">pangu-terminal-support@googlegroups.com</a>.</p>

    <p>If this policy changes, the date above changes with it.</p>

    <p class="legal-back"><%= link_to "Back to home", root_path, data: { turbo: false } %></p>
  </article>
<% end %>
